{
  "$comment": "Cross-end closure cases. One file, four sections; each section lists the ends it applies to in appliesTo, and every end must consume every section that names it. dateTimeCases: the metadata payload schema `format: date-time` check every end runs before decode, copied from ajv-formats 3.0.1 getDateTime(true) (time zone required; 'T', 't' or one whitespace separator; hour <= 23, minute <= 59, offset hour <= 23 and minute <= 59; second 60 only when the instant converted to UTC is 23:59; offset may be written +hh:mm or +hhmm; calendar date must exist). bundledInputCases: while the catalog in use is the bundled snapshot (metadataRevision 0, no online response yet) input keys are projected from the snapshot verdict exactly as an online verdict would be; there is no bundled downgrade of unavailable or kill switch to unknown. newChatDefaultCases: new chat model: lastUsedModelId if available and in userModels; else metadata defaultModelId if available and in userModels; else first available id of userModels; every tier is checked for availability first (model-retired.v1.json conversation rules); an enabled model whose own id is missing from the catalog is available only through its canonical id (userModelCanonicalIds), and only when that canonical is itself available — in models[] and not deprecated past shutdownAt, not a tombstone; hint = last_used_retired exactly when lastUsedModelId was non-null and not used. There is no connection default (isDefault) tier: connectionDefaultModelId is carried only to prove that no end reads it — an available connection default never beats lastUsedModelId or the metadata defaultModelId. relayVideoEnvelopeCases: relay transport envelopes have no video bit, so video_input is never judged by the envelope; a missing envelope (or a missing bit) is not a rejection for any key; the relay verdict is the facade-synthesized one (first-send-readpoints.v1.json: vision by connection evidence, file / video unknown/catalog_silent, wireFamily by first-send protocol; video has a family only on chat = openai_chat.video_url, other protocols have none and project as wire not implemented). Test names: CLOSURE-<id> (iOS / Android function names contain CLOSURE_<id>).",
