  "newChatAcrossConnectionsCases": {
    "appliesTo": [
      "web",
      "android",
      "ios"
    ],
    "note": "New chat without a connection scope across connections. connections are in the end's connection order (first = primary). Same chain per connection: lastUsedRef (any connection, if available and enabled) > the connection of lastUsedRef (or the primary connection when there is no lastUsedRef): its metadata defaultModelId > its first available > the following connections in order (skipping the one already tried) with an available model (its metadata default, else first available) ... > none (expect null: do not open a chat with an empty model; show the add / choose model path). Available = listed in the catalog and not retired (missing from the catalog is not available; the bundled snapshot exception stays). A connection-scoped start (detail page) never moves to another connection. Connection order: connections that cannot be used (no key, signed out) are skipped; the rest keep the user's connection list order, with the connection of lastUsedRef (or the primary connection) tried first. The hint is given only when lastUsedRef was not adopted because it is retired or missing from the catalog — not when the user disabled it, and never for connections without a catalog (subscription). The hint de-duplication key is lastUsedRef.connectionId + the raw lastUsedRef.modelId. An unscoped new chat never rewrites lastUsedRef with the fallback; it changes only when the user sends with or picks a model. When the chain returns none: with at least one connection open the model picker; with no connection go to the add-connection path. connections[].missingCredential=true = no key / signed out (skipped before every tier, the lastUsedRef tier included; no hint for a model on a skipped connection); connections[].issue=true = an errored connection (not skipped, keeps its list position). The hint predicate: lastUsedRef is on a usable connection and its model is retired or missing from the catalog (whether or not the user still has it enabled). A subscription connection while signed out is missingCredential. When the chain is empty, 'has a connection' counts only the user's own connections (official / relay / subscription). Opening a chat from a skill never rewrites lastUsedRef. expect.hint is asserted at the resolver level (the hint value the chain returns), even when modelId is null; whether the UI shows it with an empty model is the UI's concern. A connection-scoped start (detail page) on a connection with missingCredential resolves to none and its start button is hidden. lastUsedRef is written only when the user actually sends with a model or picks one (not by app start or skills).",
